% HORUS thesis bibliography (biblatex + biber; numeric-comp style per ADR-074).
%
% PROVENANCE. Each entry below is intended to be backed by a record under
% docs/sources/<type>/ per the horus-source-archival rule, carrying the same
% verified metadata so the two cannot drift apart silently. That is the standard
% this file is held to -- NOT a claim that it has always been met. See the
% correction log below, which is cumulative and is the honest statement.
%
% CORRECTION LOG. Three successive review passes each found metadata that had not
% been verified against a primary source despite an earlier blanket claim that it
% had. The claim was the defect; the entries were the symptom.
%
%   Third pass (2026-08-16) -- four entries: `fatura2` credited an author who does
%   not appear on the work; `krieger2021german` carried an invented descriptive
%   title and "and others" for a fully resolvable author list; `stberg62a` carried
%   an invented statute heading; `dsgvo32` was doing duty for two different
%   articles, sourced from a private commentary site.
%
%   Fourth pass (2026-08-17) -- one conflation: `krieger2021german` had been
%   repaired at the citation surface (authors, title, DOI, pages all verified) while
%   the corpus DESCRIPTION attributed to it -- 977 German invoices -- belongs to a
%   different paper by the same group (`thiee2023invoices`). The verified paper's
%   corpus is 1,129 English invoices. Verifying a citation's metadata is not
%   verifying the claims made about it.
%
%   Fifth pass (2026-08-18) -- three entries plus three archive defects. Entries:
%   `deepseekocr2026` carried an INVENTED title ("Improved Contexts Optical
%   Compression" appears nowhere in the work; the real subtitle is "Visual Causal
%   Flow"), and both DeepSeek entries plus `real5omnidocbench` substituted a
%   corporate name for named authors -- with `real5omnidocbench` additionally
%   attributed to OpenDataLab, which authored the PARENT benchmark rather than this
%   extension. Archive side: `edge2024graphrag` and `dsgvo28` had NO record at all
%   (the nearest files covered a different artefact -- a library, and a different
%   article), and the `dsgvo32` record still pointed at the private commentary site
%   the third pass had moved the ENTRY away from. Each is repaired in place, with
%   the correction recorded next to the entry and in the archive record.
%
% All repairs above are in place. The number of passes it took is the point worth
% keeping: the lesson is the one Chapter 6 makes about field specifications -- a
% claim of verification is itself a claim to be checked, and a comment asserting
% verification does not perform it. Every pass that trusted the previous pass's
% assertion instead of re-deriving it found something the previous pass had missed.
%
% Entries are grouped by role in the argument, not alphabetically -- biblatex
% sorts the printed bibliography, so grouping here is purely for maintenance.
%
% RULE: do not add an entry here without first creating or completing its record
% under docs/sources/. A citation whose archive record says "authors TBD" is a
% citation this project is not entitled to make.
%
